  "instruction": "Use ANSYS Workbench to complete a Static Structural analysis. Physical problem: A square plate with four simply supported edges is subjected to a uniform pressure load. Coordinate system and geometry: - Use the global Cartesian coordinate system. - Model the plate mid-surface in the global X-Y plane. - The out-of-plane direction is the global Z direction. - The square plate mid-surface occupies: - 0 ≤ X ≤ 100 mm - 0 ≤ Y ≤ 100 mm - Z = 0 mm - The plate thickness is 1 mm. - Use a shell or surface-body plate model with assigned thickness 1 mm. Model parameters: - Plate size: 100 mm × 100 mm - Plate thickness: 1 mm - Material: Structural Steel with the following linear elastic properties: - Young's modulus E = 210000 MPa - Poisson's ratio ν = 0.3 - Mesh: - Face element size: 5 mm - Use a mapped or regular quadrilateral-dominant mesh where possible. Boundary conditions: - Apply simply supported boundary conditions on all four plate edges. - On the edges at X = 0, X = 100 mm, Y = 0, and Y = 100 mm: - Constrain only the out-of-plane displacement UZ = 0. - Do not fully fix the edges. - Add only the minimum in-plane constraints required to prevent rigid-body motion. Load: - Apply a uniform pressure of 0.1 MPa to the plate surface. - The pressure should act in the negative global Z direction. Analysis type: - Static Structural analysis. Save requirements: - Use C:\\Users\\user\\Desktop as the working location. - Save the Workbench project file as: C:\\Users\\user\\Desktop\\wb_plate.wbpj - Save the MAPDL-equivalent database file as: C:\\Users\\user\\Desktop\\wb_plate.db - Save the MAPDL-equivalent structural result file as: C:\\Users\\user\\Desktop\\wb_plate.rst Run the solver to completion and ensure a result file is generated.",
